# Everything listed here is excluded from the build context -- the tarball the
# CLI ships to the daemon before the build starts.
#
# Two reasons this file matters:
#
# 1. SPEED. Without it, `COPY . .` uploads and copies node_modules from your
#    host. On this tiny project that is annoying; on a real one it is hundreds
#    of megabytes on every single build.
#
# 2. SECRETS. Without it, `COPY . .` bakes your .env into an image layer. Layers
#    are permanent: deleting the file in a later RUN does not remove it, it just
#    hides it. Anyone who pulls the image can extract it with `docker history`
#    or by unpacking the layer. Day 5 covers this properly.

node_modules
npm-debug.log
.npm

.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
*.md

.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
